  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">South Senegal Rice on the Rise</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to increase the income and resilience of 30,000 smallholder rice farmers (of which over 20,000 women), in the Casamance region in southern Senegal by using a market-led approach to improve productivity, facilitate access to adapted financial and nonfinancial services and secured market, while simultaneously contributing to local and national food security.In addition, the 30,000 farmers will have improved resilience and capacity to cope with climate, financial and market shocks.</narrative>
  </description>
